            <div xml:id="d94">

                <pb facs="0245" n="117" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg117"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.9412Anti-War/48: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Neville</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-07-18T18:00:00+09:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 18, 1928—6
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received July 18—8:48
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>86. My telegram No. 83, July 9, 2 p.m.<anchor n="99" xml:id="d94-f1"/> Foreign
                    Minister told me today that the question of wording is still causing some
                    difficulty in the Government. He said that this is the only reason for Japanese
                    Parliament’s delay in answering, but he hoped to be able to reply favorably in a
                    few days.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Neville</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
